 "notes_for_editor": "Primary reports before 1891 are not in the corpus, so the 1850s-80s chronology rests on Pepper (modern, uses station logs). Disagreements stated in text: original lens order (Pepper sixth vs USLHS fourth), lens arc, Wheatley body found 21 May vs 21 June (and Pepper/LHF spell his companion Braidon/Brandon, newspaper OCR Hrandon), Kimball retirement 20 vs 30 April 1925 and age, Leuty date 31 Oct vs 1 Nov. Registry record height 12 m vs Pepper 38 ft 9 in tower not reconciled. NRHP PDF not digitised; only the NPGallery metadata cited. Roster parsed from USLHS lines; Curry/Currie, Clarke/Clark and Kimball name variants differ across sources. Mining Gazette quote is as quoted by Pepper. Kimball's retirement bulletin text has soft hyphens in OCR. Fact-check 2026-10-22: red-paint date disagrees (1911 in Pepper/LHF, 1965 in museum history); stated in text. Pepper's 'age 66, 43 years' for Kimball is inconsistent with his own entry date (1872, age 18) and the Bulletin (age 71, nearly 53 years); text follows the Bulletin.",
